      "message": "\"They are deterministic, so a hash does not change between runs\" holds for the content hashes (numbers, strings, bytevectors, symbols), but not for the identity ones. `eq-hash` and `eqv-hash` of a heap object come from its address, and so does `equal-hash` of anything that reaches a record or a procedure, so they can differ from run to run. The commit message says the same. Worth narrowing to the content hashes, so nobody counts on a stable iteration order for an `eq?` table.",
